	"Name": "ScheduledSearch - Okta - Policy - Application - Okta Application Access Denied by Sign-On Policy",
	"Description": "An application sign-on policy denied access. This is the policy working as intended, but a run of denials against one account or from one address is worth a look: it means something is repeatedly trying to reach an application it cannot satisfy the policy for.\n\nEvent type: application.policy.sign_on.deny_access\n\nReference(s):\n- https://developer.okta.com/docs/reference/api/event-types/\n- https://developer.okta.com/docs/api/openapi/okta-management/management/tag/SystemLog/\n\nThis scheduled search is a dispatcher on \"Alert - Okta - Alert Router\". Its name is what appears as the alert name, so rename it here if you want the alerts named differently.\n\nIt ships disabled; enable it once you have reviewed the query and are happy with the volume it produces.",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	],
